      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2011 The Authors. Internal Medicine Journal © 2011 Royal Australasian College of Physicians.",
        "AbstractText": "A 45-year-old man with heterozygous Factor V Leiden presented with his third cerebrovascular accident despite being on warfarin at a therapeutic international normalized ratio. Subsequent investigation revealed a second genetic diagnosis of Fabry disease. He then had an acute myocardial infarction whilst on aspirin and warfarin."
      },
